UID:7e49d1a9f2aea4fe@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260805T032933Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260804
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] New MaineCare Partner Portal Training for Tra
 ding Partners
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			New MaineCare Partner Portal Training for Trading Partn
 ers\nNew MaineCare Partner Portal Training for Trading Partners\nAug 04\, 
 2026\nWe\npreviously shared\nthat a refreshed and upgraded MIHMS\, with a
  new “MaineCare Partner Portal\,” is coming in October 2026. This w
 ill replace the current HealthPAS Online Portal. We are now inviting 
 trading partners to register for training starting September 8\, 2026\,
  to help you prepare for the transition to the new portal.\nGainwell Tec
 hnologies will be leading live virtual instructor-led training sessions.
  These courses will provide the knowledge and skills needed to navigate
  the new portal\, complete daily business functions\, and use new porta
 l features. Training demonstrations\, materials\, and supporting resource
 s will help participants prepare for a successful transition.\nSteps You N
 eed to Take to Attend Training\nReview the available training topics list
 ed below and identify the sessions that align with your role and respon
 sibilities.\nUse the Learning Management System (LMS) registration to c
 reate an account\, access the training catalog\, and enroll in applicable
  sessions. See the instructions below for guidance in registering.\nCont
 act Gainwell (instructions below) if you need assistance.\nRecorded sessi
 ons and other training materials will be available in the LMS after traini
 ng sessions for ongoing reference.\nMaineCare Partner Portal Training Ses
 sions\nCourse Name\nDescription\nME - TPT - Migrated Trading Partner Log 
 In and Account Maintenance Training (ILC)\nLearn how to complete first-ti
 me login activities\, configure multi-factor authentication (MFA)\, manage
  user accounts and permissions\, perform account maintenance activities\, 
 and understand electronic data interchange (EDI) certification requirement
 s and status monitoring.\nThis course is only for Admin (R7) users.\nME - 
 TPT - Trading Partner Registration \nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/provid
 ers/provider-bulletins/new-mainecare-partner-portal-training-trading-partn
 ers-2026-08-04
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/new-mainec
 are-partner-portal-training-trading-partners-2026-08-04
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:7269744952375279@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260804T195536Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260804
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] MHRC Guidance on HUD Change to Definition of 
 Assistance Animal
DESCRIPTION:Maine Human Rights Commission \n# 51 State House Station\, Aug
 usta\, ME 04333-0051 \nPhysical location: 19 Union Street\, Augusta\, ME 0
 4330 \n■ ■Phone (207) 624-6290 Fax (207) 624-8729  TTY: Maine Relay 71
 1 \nwww.maine.gov/mhrc \nKit Thomson Crossman Barbara Archer Hirsch \nEXEC
 UTIVE DIRECTOR COMMISSION COUNSEL \nMAINE HUMAN RIGHTS COMMISSION \nPublic
  Guidance Statement RE: HUD's New Emotional Support Animal Enforcement Gui
 dance and \nMaine Housing Providers' Continuing Obligations Under the Main
 e Human Rights Act \nAugust 4\, 2026 \nWhat Has Changed at the Federal Lev
 el \nOn May 22\, 2026\, the U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Developme
 nt (HUD) issued an enforcement \nmemorandum announcing that it will no lon
 ger find reasonable cause in housing complaints involving \nemotional supp
 ort animals (ESAs). In other words\, animals that provide comfort\, compan
 ionship\, or otherwise \nmitigate the effects of a person’s disability b
 ut have not been individually trained to perform specific \ndisability-rel
 ated tasks are no longer protected at the federal level. Going forward\, H
 UD will pursue \nenforcement only where an animal has been trained to perf
 orm work or tasks directly related to a person's \ndisability (essentially
 \, HUD has imported the Americans with Disabilities Act's narrower "servic
 e animal" \ndefinition into Fair Housing Act enforcement). \nHUD simultane
 ously rescinded its 2020 guidance\, which had for years provided meaningfu
 l protections to \nindividuals who rely on ESAs as part of their disabilit
 y-related care. After 35 years without updating its \nregulations in this 
 area\, the federal government's chosen solution has been\, perhaps unsurpr
 isingly\, to reduce \nprotections rather than clarify them. \nThe Maine Hu
 man Rights Commission takes note of this development. We also take note th
 at it changes \nnothing in Maine. \nWhat Has NOT Changed: Your Rights Unde
 r the Maine Human Rights Act \nThe Maine Human Rights Act (MHRA)\, 5 M.R.S
 .A. ch. 337\, is an independent state law. It is not subordinate \nhttps:/
 /www.maine.gov/mhrc/sites/maine.gov.mhrc/files/inline-files/MHRC%20Guidanc
 e%20on%20HUD%20Assistance%20Animal%20Change.pdf
URL:https://www.maine.gov/mhrc/sites/maine.gov.mhrc/files/inline-files/MHR
 C%20Guidance%20on%20HUD%20Assistance%20Animal%20Change.pdf
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:4c824fbd45f2175f@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260804T195451Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260804
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Upcoming Pause in Configuration Changes
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Upcoming Pause in Configuration Changes\nUpcoming Pause
  in Configuration Changes\nAug 04\, 2026\nAs\npreviously communicated\n\, 
 the Office of MaineCare Services is launching an upgraded MIHMS\, our clai
 ms processing system\, in October 2026. To support system readiness activi
 ties\, MaineCare is temporarily pausing the implementation of configuratio
 n changes from the end of August to the end of October.\nCoding and NDC Re
 quests\nContinue submitting coding requests to\nOMS.referencefile@maine.go
 v\nand NDC/J-Code Requests to\nMaineCareNDCrequest.DHHS@maine.gov\n. Reque
 sts submitted by August 19\, 2026\, if approved\, will be implemented no l
 ater than the last synchronization on August 25\, 2026. Continue to submit
  these requests as usual after these dates. MaineCare will review and docu
 ment change requests beginning at the end of October.\nRate Change Request
 s\nContinue submitting rate change requests as usual to\nMIHMSRateRqst.DHH
 S@maine.gov\nthroughout this period. MaineCare will review and document ch
 ange requests as appropriate for implementation beginning at the end of Oc
 tober.\nClaims and Billing Inquiries\nContinue directing claims and billin
 g inquiries to Provider Services at 1-866-690-5585. We will continue revie
 wing claim denials to determine if a configuration change is needed. Maine
 Care will review and document change requests as appropriate for implement
 ation before the configuration pause or beginning at the end of October.\n
 We appreciate your continued cooperation during this transition. If you ha
 ve questions about the configuration pause or the status of a request\, pl
 ease contact\nyou\nr\nProvider Relations Specialist\n.\nhttps://www.maine.
 gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/upcoming-pause-configuration-cha
 nges-2026-08-04
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/upcoming-p
 ause-configuration-changes-2026-08-04
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:c5e9fc0a690bb4d0@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260804T143723Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260804
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] 8/4/2026: Maine eCourts Scheduled to be Imple
 mented in  Cumberland County Courts in September
DESCRIPTION:Home\nSkip to top navigation\nSkip to side navigation\nSkip to
  content\nSkip to footer\nMaine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp
 \n|\nSearch Maine.gov\nCOURT ALERTS IN EFFECT.\nSee Active Alerts\nHome\n
 →\nNews & Announcements\nMaine eCourts Scheduled to be Implemented in  C
 umberland County Courts in September\nDate:\n8/4/2026\nThe Maine Judicial 
 Branch announced today that the schedule for transitioning courts in Cumbe
 rland County (comprising Judicial Region 2) from paper filing to electroni
 c filing (eFiling) is scheduled for Monday\, September 28\, 2026. The next
  implementation includes all case types in the Cumberland County Unified C
 riminal Docket (UCD)\, Cumberland County Superior Court\, Portland Distric
 t Court\, and Bridgton District Court.\nAttorneys\, government agencies (e
 xcept law enforcement agencies)\, and parties who file more than six non-e
 mergency cases in a calendar year\, are required to eFile in courts that h
 ave implemented Maine eCourts. Self-represented parties are not required t
 o eFile and can continue to file documents as they always have\, in paper 
 at the courthouse\, by mail\, or by email if filing a protection from abus
 e or harassment case.\nAttorneys and other required eFilers should prepare
  in advance for the transition\, and take note of upcoming presentation an
 d trainings:\nPresentation for Cumberland County Legal Professionals and S
 takeholders\nThe Maine Judicial Branch will hold a virtual presentation by
  ZOOM on August 10th\, at noon to discuss the implementation of Maine eCou
 rts and electronic filing (eFiling) in Judicial Region 2\, Cumberland Coun
 ty Courts. Attorneys and other professional filers are encouraged to atten
 d.\nTopic: Maine eCourts in Region 2: Cumberland County\nDate & Time: Mond
 ay\, August 10\, 2026 at 12:00 p.m.\nPlease click the link below to join t
 he webinar:\nhttps://courts-maine-gov.zoom.us/j/94955753059\nPasscode: 993
 548\nThe webinar will be recorded and made available on the Judicial Branc
 h website on the Maine eCourts Training & Resources page followi\nhttps://
 www.courts.maine.gov/news/article.html?id=13357575
URL:https://www.courts.maine.gov/news/article.html?id=13357575
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
