SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Maine voters can request absentee ballots for
  Nov. 3 election starting today\; Ballots will be mailed beginning 30 days
  before the Election
DESCRIPTION:AUGUSTA\, MAINE\n– The Secretary of State’s Office today a
 nnounced that Maine voters may now request absentee ballots for the Novemb
 er 3\, 2026 General Election. Voters may\nrequest ballots online\nor by co
 ntacting their town or city clerk. Contact\ninformation for municipal cler
 ks\ncan be found on the Secretary of State website.\nMaine’s no-excuse a
 bsentee voting laws allows any registered voter to request a ballot three 
 months before Election Day\, and their ballots will be issued by their mun
 icipal clerks beginning 30 days prior to Election Day. Once a ballot reque
 st is submitted\, Maine voters can\ntrack the process of that request and 
 their ballot\nonline.\nMaine’s no-excuse absentee voting period\, includ
 ing in-person absentee voting at town and city halls\, extends through Oct
 ober 29. All absentee ballots for the upcoming General Election must be re
 ceived by a voter’s municipality by 8 p.m. on November 3\, 2026.\n###\nh
 ttps://www.maine.gov/sos/news/maine-voters-can-request-absentee-ballots-no
 v-3-election-starting-today-ballots-will-be-mailed
URL:https://www.maine.gov/sos/news/maine-voters-can-request-absentee-ballo
 ts-nov-3-election-starting-today-ballots-will-be-mailed
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
